---
title: Turkey and Zucchini Burgers with Scallion and Cumin
description: Small herb-flecked turkey and zucchini burgers, seared then finished in the oven, with a sharp sour cream and sumac sauce.
tags: [make-ahead]
course: main
icons: [drumstick, leaf, pan-frying]
cuisine: Middle Eastern
source:
  name: Ottolenghi
  book: Jerusalem
  author: Yotam Ottolenghi and Sami Tamimi
  url: https://ottolenghi.co.uk/pages/recipes/turkey-courgette-burgers-spring-onion-cumin
servings: 4
yield: 18%burgers
---

= Sour Cream and Sumac Sauce

In a #small bowl{}, stir together the @sour cream{100%g}, @Greek yogurt{150%g}, @lemon zest{1%tsp}(grated), @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @garlic cloves{1}(crushed, a small one for the sauce), @olive oil{1 1/2%tbsp}, @sumac{1%tbsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}. Set aside, or chill until you need it.

> **Making ahead** — The sauce keeps in the fridge, and a double batch is worth having for grilled vegetables or fritters. It mellows after a day, so taste it and add more sumac and lemon juice if it needs them.

= Burgers

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C). Line a #baking sheet{} with #parchment paper{}.

In a #large bowl{}, combine the @ground turkey{500%g}, @zucchini{1}(large, coarsely grated, about 200 g), @scallions{40%g}(thinly sliced), @egg{1}, @mint{2%tbsp}(chopped), @cilantro{2%tbsp}(chopped), @&garlic cloves{2}, crushed, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @&salt{1%tsp}, @&black pepper{1/2%tsp}, coarsely ground, and @cayenne{1/2%tsp}. Mix with your hands until even.

Shape the mixture into small burgers of about 45 g each. You should get about 18.

Pour enough @sunflower oil{100%ml}(about, for searing) into a #large frying pan{} to cover the bottom in a thin layer, about 2 mm deep. Get it properly hot over medium heat.

Sear the burgers in batches, turning them until golden brown on all sides, about ~sear{4%minutes} per batch. Add more oil as the pan needs it.

Move the seared burgers to the lined baking sheet and bake for ~bake{5-7%minutes}, until just cooked through.

Serve warm or at room temperature, with the sauce on the side.

> **Packing them up** — These travel well, so extras are good for lunchboxes and snacks.
